  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential mechanism linking [(3S,8S,9R,10R,12R,13S,14R,17R)-17-acetyl-3,8,14-trihydroxy-10,13-dimethyl-2,3,4,7,9,11,12,15,16,17-decahydro-1H-cyclopenta[a]phenanthren-12-yl] benzoate to SNB-78 through a shared target, VMRC-LCP. This compound is identified as a target of multiple agents, including Ginsenoside R10 and Cycloeudesmol, which both interact with VMRC-LCP and ultimately lead to SNB-78. The evidence suggests that the compound may act through a common pathway involving VMRC-LCP, potentially modulating cellular processes that are relevant to SNB-78's biological function. The integration of multiple targets and their shared interaction with VMRC-LCP supports a mechanistic link, though the exact mode of action remains to be fully elucidated. The presence of multiple agents targeting VMRC-LCP implies that the compound may exert its effects through a broader, yet consistent, biological mechanism.",
